## Steps

### Step 1: Produce `docs/c-ref-se1-file.md`

Launch a Sonnet agent to read the C source and produce the reference doc. Agent brief:
- Read `sweph.h`: `struct plan_data` (all fields, offsets), `struct file_data`, SEI_* body constants (SEI_SUN=0..SEI_NPLANETS), SEI_FLG_* flags, SEI_FILE_* file type constants
- Read `sweph.c`: `read_const()` function (~lines 3700-4200) — the complete header parsing logic: magic/version string format, byte-order detection mechanism, field-by-field reading sequence, per-planet metadata loop
- Extract: exact binary layout (which bytes, what order), how npl (planet count) is determined per file type, how `lndx0`/`nndx` file offsets are computed
- Follow format of `docs/c-ref-nutation.md`

